From a8438b3a75c86ac7b2aea296a55b980027d90c97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cole Morgan <colerussellmorgan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:42:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] FieldBleSync: BLE peripheral relay for KOReader sync via
 a phone

New library implementing the Field Sync protocol v1 (reader side):
chunk framing with reassembly (16 KB cap, 5 s gap timeout, FIRST
resets), hello/req/res/bye/error messages, a RelayTransport that sends
one request at a time and waits up to 30 s for the matching response,
and a NimBLE GATT peripheral (FIELD_BLE_SYNC builds only) with an
encrypted, MITM-authenticated, bonded link, DisplayOnly passkey,
FieldSync-XXXX advertising with a 60 s timeout and full stack teardown.

Host tests cover the framing vectors from the protocol, oversize,
timeout and FIRST-reset handling, message escaping and parsing, and the
relay's request/response matching against a fake link.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
